      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:107:13",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ النَّبِيُّ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) طُوبَى لِلْمَسَاكِينِ بِالصَّبْرِ وَ هُمُ الَّذِينَ يَرَوْنَ مَلَكُوتَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَ الْأَرْضِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The Prophet<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘Tooba is for the poor ones due to the patience, and they are those who would be shown the Kingdoms of the skies and the earth’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "13. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from al-Nawfali from al-Sakuni from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “The Holy Prophet has said, ‘Tuba (a tree in paradise) is for the destitutes who bear patience and they are the ones who observe the kingdom of heavens and earth.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
